@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor "Administrator / Pharmacist" as Staff

node "Vercel / Browser Client" as Client {
  component "React 19 SPA\nTypeScript, React Router\nZustand, Axios, JWT refresh" as Web
}

node "Render Web Service\nDocker · ASP.NET Core 8" as Backend {
  component "API Layer\nControllers, JWT and role authorization,\nCORS and exception handling" as Api
  component "Application Layer\nServices, MediatR commands/queries,\nvalidation and DTO mapping" as App
  component "Domain Layer\nEntities, business rules, enums,\nexceptions and repository contracts" as Domain
  component "Persistence Layer\nEF Core, AppDbContext, repositories,\nUnit of Work and migrations" as Persistence
  component "Infrastructure Adapters\nSMTP email, file storage, backup,\nmonitoring and logging" as Infrastructure
  component "Hosted Background Services\nExpiry checks, notification checks,\nretention cleanup" as Jobs
}

database "Render PostgreSQL\nNpgsql" as Database
cloud "SMTP Email Provider" as SMTP
cloud "AWS S3\n(local storage provider also supported)" as S3

Staff --> Web : uses browser UI
Web --> Api : HTTPS · REST/JSON\nBearer JWT
Api --> App : dispatch request
App --> Domain : applies rules
App --> Persistence : reads and writes
Persistence --> Database : EF Core / Npgsql
App ..> Infrastructure : injected service adapters
Jobs --> App : scheduled workflows
Infrastructure --> SMTP : password reset email
Infrastructure --> S3 : file storage

note bottom of Backend
  The backend modules and hosted services run together
  in one ASP.NET Core API process (modular monolith).
end note
@enduml
